Limitations. This report is a desk-based study that relies on published audit findings and parliamentary records. It does not use access to PMEC data, and the proposed design still has to be tested in pilot districts before conclusions can be drawn about its effect on payroll accuracy. The figures are quoted as reported in the sources, and an officer who could not be accounted for is not by itself evidence of fraud.
Future work. Further work should pilot the system in selected districts, measure indicators such as the share of records matched to verified stations and the time taken to resolve cases (Section 2.9), and examine integration with national identity and bank data, subject to data protection requirements.
